    <string name="settings_safety_guidelines">Campus Safety &amp; Handover Rules</string>
    <string name="settings_safety_description">Recommended handover locations &amp; verification tips</string>
    <string name="settings_safety_understood">Got it</string>
    <string name="settings_safety_message">Meet in public.\n\n• Pick an active, well-lit place on campus such as the Octagon, a library entrance or the Admin Quad. Avoid quiet corridors, basements and parking areas after dark.\n\n• Drop a pin inside campus grounds so you both know where to meet.\n\n• Check the verification answer before handing anything over. If it does not match, do not meet up — decline the claim instead.\n\n• Keep the conversation in the app chat until you are actually face to face.\n\n• Never share your phone number, address or payment details in a report or claim.\n\nIf a meetup or message feels wrong, decline the claim and use \"Report this post\" to flag it to moderators.</string>
    <string name="settings_report_problem">Report a Problem</string>
    <string name="settings_report_problem_description">Flag a post or report inaccurate information</string>
    <string name="settings_report_problem_message">Use the \"Report this post\" option on any report to flag it to moderators. For anything else, contact your campus IT help desk.</string>
    <string name="settings_report_problem_understood">Understood</string>

    <string name="settings_privacy">Privacy &amp; Security</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_description">How your data is stored and protected</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_message">Your session is stored encrypted on this device.\n\nReports and claims are protected by PostgreSQL Row Level Security, so only you and the people involved in a claim can read them.\n\nYour email address is never shown on reports. Verification notes and handover details stay private to you and the report owner.</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_understood">Got it</string>

